body:
Proposed in research/reports/ml_signals_2026-11-12.md (Rule candidates block), for the orchestrator to merge into rules.yaml after review:
R-ML-1 prefer log-HAR level x forecast-day weekday for next-day crypto variance (B, provisional; register vol.har_dow);
R-ML-2 expect a smaller weekend discount in high vol (C, provisional; register a direct test);
R-ML-3 avoid jump / semivariance / range / raw-return inputs for daily variance (B);
R-ML-4 prefer boosted trees for CENTRAL next-day expectations only after a forward test (C, provisional);
R-ML-5 avoid NN / tree direction models on standard features (B);
R-ML-6 explain vol forecasts with grouped TreeSHAP, not network features (B).
Questions to register before use: market-wide down day -> higher next-day vol (TreeSHAP sign, contradicts V11 at factor level?); up-trend -> higher vol.

Agent D (sparsity). Fixed before any test result was looked at. Full spec in the docstring of src/ai_trader/research/sparsity_study.py.

H-SP1 (lottery ticket). Full monthly walk-forward, no subset: 56 refits 2022-04..2026-11, the same rows, purge, validation block, standardisation, config and 3 seeds as H-NN1. Dense = ml.sparse.train_masked with no mask. It is bit-identical to models.fit_mlp (max |diff| 0 on the 2026-07 refit). Pruning: iterative magnitude pruning, layer-wise, 20% of the surviving hidden weights and 10% of the head per round, biases never pruned, at least 1 weight per layer kept. Rewind to the end of epoch 1 (weights and batch order), fresh AdamW, mask re-applied after every step. 22 rounds; sparsity is deterministic: 95.4% at round 14 (the test level), 98.4% at 19, 99.04% at 22. Forecast per round = exp(mean of the 3 members' log forecasts + validation-block c). Ratio = date-averaged QLIKE sparse / dense, 10-day block bootstrap, 1000 draws. Segment: supports iff ratio <= 1.01 and CI upper <= 1.02. Contradicts iff ratio > 1.02 or CI lower > 1.01. Pooled: both segments must support. p = P*(ratio >= 1.02). Direction: the same pruning, Brier skill per round, descriptive only.

H-SP2 (stability selection). Library of 236 columns:
- the 52 inputs;
- 35 signed logs;
- 49 exact-calendar lags: lrv_d 1-30, |ret| 1-7, market log RV 1-7, ret 1-5;
- 45 products of the H-NN3 in-sample top-10 inputs;
- 48 upper-quantile indicators of 12 inputs, edges from in-sample rows;
- 7 weekday dummies.
Target: next-day log RV. Per segment: 200 subsamples of half the dates, randomised lasso with W ~ U[0.5, 1], a 40-value lambda grid. Lambda region: the mean union size stays <= q_max = sqrt(0.6 p), which gives E[V] <= 1. pi_thr = 0.8. Segment: supports iff 1 <= |S| <= 10. Pooled: additionally needs Jaccard overlap >= 0.7. Holm p = hypergeometric overlap p.

H-SP3 (surviving neurons). Network: the seed-0 member of the 2026-07 refit (labels to 2026-06-30, as H-NN4), at the highest of the 95/98/99% rounds that passes H-SP1 in both segments (95% if none). Units: cubic-spline GAM on the best single input and the best additive pair, both chosen in-sample. Holdout R^2 of the pair > 0.8 is required for >= 80% of evaluable units. Ablation: the top-3 units by in-sample |act x grad| are mean-ablated. Required: QLIKE ratio > 1.05 with CI lower > 1.00. Pooled = clean_holdout. Holm within SP over SP1-3 per segment.

Built the Rust side of docs/EXECUTION_PIPELINE.md. at-risk::decide(intent, account, portfolio, rules, cfg) is a pure function. It sizes at fixed risk from entry/stop/equity with the fees.yaml round trip included, and checks every rule, reporting each violation by name: kill_switch, gate_blocked, daily_loss_limit, max_new_trades_per_day, max_open_positions, max_positions_per_cluster (family = cluster, R-PD-1), duplicate_symbol, max_gross_exposure, exceeds_max_leverage, stop_too_far, stop_inside_min_sigma / stop_beyond_max_sigma (|ln(entry/stop)|/sigma.per_bar, no weekday shrink, R-VOL-2), missing_sigma, net_er_below_min / net_er_missing (the engine checks the lower of its own recomputation and K net_er_r), below_min_qty, below_min_notional, invalid_intent, unknown_instrument, no_position_to_close, stale_intent and duplicate_intent. A gate reduce sizes at 0.5R. A flat intent closes only that strategy position and is never blocked.

at-exec PaperBook fills conservatively:
- market entries at the next open plus slippage (taker), cancelled if that open is already through the stop or target;
- limit entries only when the bar trades through them (maker), with a TTL;
- resting stops (R-EXEC-1) on the bar low/high, stop first when stop and target share a bar, gaps filled at the open;
- targets at the target price as taker;
- KILL cancels and flattens.

The new config/fees.yaml sets crypto maker 2 / taker 5.5 bp and TradFi maker 0 / taker 2.75 bp, with 2 bp slippage per market leg for both.

atx exec-intents runs replay or paper and refuses live mode and mainnet. Decision times are rounded up to the bar grid, so decisions are point in time. It writes data/exec/decisions/<run>.jsonl and data/exec/paper/<run>/ and journals the run.

Smoke test on the real lake with $100 equity: qty rounding leaves trades at about 0.5R, not 1R, and BTC/ETH fall below min_qty. Small accounts are lot-limited, which matters when reading paper R.

Built crates/at-match: a deterministic limit order book with Bybit v5 documented semantics, and atx match-sim (JSONL in; trades, ob200-shaped book, rejects and stats out). It is a simulator only, with no network code.

Semantics:
- price-time FIFO priority; a partial fill keeps its place; an amend that changes price or raises qty loses priority, one that lowers qty keeps it;
- GTC, IOC, FOK (exact pre-check) and PostOnly (EC_PostOnlyWillTakeLiquidity);
- market orders run as protected IOC limits: ask1 x (1 + pct) or ask1 + n ticks; the default 1% band is an assumption;
- reduce-only against a per-owner ledger: rejected when nothing would be reduced; qty cut to the position; resting reduce-only orders trimmed, furthest from the market first; never flips a position;
- named filter rejects; maker and taker fees from config/fees.yaml.

Verified:
- 23 unit tests;
- invariants checked after every operation on 12 random flows;
- trade-for-trade equality with a naive reference matcher on 6 flows;
- a synthetic one-minute ob200 replay that leaves the engine book equal to the message book after every message;
- book.jsonl read unchanged by sim/book.py, with no u gaps and no crossed bins.

Engine benchmark: 3.79M order events/s on one core with about 270 levels per side; the JSONL driver runs at 0.62M lines/s.

Not covered: Bybit internals such as liquidation, ADL, mark-price limits, SMP groups, RPI and latency. Assumptions are listed in the crate docs.

The real ob200 replay test has not been run, because no ob200 file is on disk. It runs when AT_MATCH_OB200 is set.

Pre-declaration, written before the first live v3 line. From the next hourly run (scripts/live_nn.py at hh:03), the frozen cross-sectional network v3 runs live as CONTEXT ONLY, after v1, v2.1 and players. It is wrapped so a v3 failure cannot stop or change v1 / v2.1; tests check that their files are byte-identical with v3 on or off.

Not a signal (R-XS-2 / R-XS-3). The relative-return ranking is mostly a low-vol ranking, and its top-minus-bottom spread is negative after costs in both segments. Nothing in the decision path reads it: agent.decision reads only the live_nn line. It carries no sizes. The only head with a holdout gain over the incumbent is the 1h vol head (R-XS-1); it is shown next to v1 and panel log-HAR-t.

Track record (principle 8; changing any of these starts a new record):
- model_id xs.v3, version xs_v3-2026Q4, tool live_xs_v3.1;
- spec.json sha256 cfb9ba3579e9a3b45f5e8a8e941aa6ecbe94956e5273b9336681a0cfed1f0ed2;
- weights v3_seed0.pt 94bcf0ae7897c2c2..., v3_seed1.pt 985fd325147f0853..., v3_seed2.pt 471b0b4d5a5281ac...; every run checks them against spec.files_sha256, plus the four source files against spec.code_sha256, and stops v3 on a mismatch;
- token-map projection data/models/xs_v3/live/projection.json sha256 3be40e896ee6ad8e2d7dd3d75391e7a68d771dd3d78fb81722f37a0041e76ca1. It was fitted once on the refit's fit block (39,833 h): PCA of the three seeds' concatenated [z, a]; PC1 80%, PC2 12%. It is never refit live;
- live module src/ai_trader/live/xs_v3.py sha256 5b179c1e722f2ac8...; each line logs it.

Inputs: every run calls the study's own token_rows and assemble, and does not re-implement features. Two speed-ups, both exact:
- the expanding hour-of-week profiles are evaluated on the tail only;
- two market_frame recursions whose columns v3 never reads are skipped.

Check: live rows rebuilt at as_of 2026-11-14 20:03 and 2026-11-13 00:03 equal the study panel bitwise (X, M and present). The seed-averaged quantiles match the 2026Q4 walk-forward predictions to 1.6e-7. Runtime is about 13-16 s, at 2 torch threads.

Logged per hour, all 23 universe-L tokens (absent tokens masked as in training):
- 1h / 4h |r| quantiles of v3 and of log-HAR-t;
- 4h / 24h relative-return q10 / q50 / q90 and the 80% ACI band. The 24h band is labelled as known to under-cover (holdout 0.749);
- the rank by rel median next to the low-vol rank (-lsig2);
- map coordinates and attention, both descriptive (R-XS-4).

Scored once each window closes:
- 1h / 4h vol pinball v3 vs log-HAR-t, and q90 coverage;
- 4h / 24h rank IC of v3 and of low vol;
- ACI / raw band hits.

ACI is updated only at the study's non-overlapping origins: 4h at 00, 04, ... UTC; 24h at 00 UTC. Pre-stated reading: the forward v3 IC is expected near the low-vol IC (holdout 4h 0.052 vs 0.039, 24h 0.061 vs 0.060). A forward quarter with a positive gross spread or a momentum IC above zero would trigger the R-XS-2 review. Nothing here changes R-XS-3.
